IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc1-part4-amounts`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 4, the maximum amount, the child element and the housing costs
-- element: regulations 23 to 26.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- WHAT IS HERE: which amounts make up the maximum amount of an award (regulation 23), the child element and its additional
-- amount for a disabled child (regulation 24), the three conditions for the housing costs element (regulation 25) and which
-- Schedule works out its amount (regulation 26). The amounts themselves are regulation 36's (uc1-part4-amounts.l4).
-- Schedules 1 to 5 are uc3's: wherever a condition rests on one of them, whether it holds is a plain input, commented
-- "out of range: Schedule N (piece uc3)".
-- Money is a NUMBER of pounds.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 23: the elements. The core names them (`Element of an award`).

-- (2) The elements included under section 12 of the Act (particular needs or circumstances): the LCWRA element, the carer element
-- and the childcare costs element.
-- src:505 | (2) The elements to be included in an award under section 12 of the Act in respect of particular needs or circumstances are—
-- src:506 | (a) ... the LCWRA element (see regulations 27 to 28);
-- src:507 | (b) the carer element (see regulations 29 and 30); and
-- src:508 | (c) the childcare costs element (see regulations 31 to 35).
@ref reg 23(2) (src:505-508)
GIVEN element IS AN `Element of an award`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23(2) — an element included under section 12 of the Act` element MEANS
    CONSIDER element
    WHEN `standard allowance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `child element` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `housing costs element` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `LCWRA element` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `carer element` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `childcare costs element` THEN TRUE

-- (1) The amounts under sections 9 to 12 of the Act make up the maximum amount of an award (section 8(2) of the Act is not
-- among the inputs, so the sum is the one regulation 23(1) describes). An element the award does not include is an amount of nil.
-- src:499 | (1) This Part contains provisions about the amounts (“the elements”) under—
-- src:500 | (a) section 9 (the standard allowance);
-- src:501 | (b) section 10 (responsibility for children and young persons);
-- src:502 | (c) section 11 (housing costs); and
-- src:503 | (d) section 12 (particular needs and circumstances),
-- src:504 | of the Act that make up the maximum amount of an award of universal credit, as provided in section 8(2) of the Act.
@ref reg 23(1) (src:499-504)
DECLARE `Amounts of the elements of an award` HAS
    `the standard allowance`        IS A NUMBER
    `the child element`             IS A NUMBER
    `the housing costs element`     IS A NUMBER
    `the LCWRA element`             IS A NUMBER
    `the carer element`             IS A NUMBER
    `the childcare costs element`   IS A NUMBER

-- src:499 | (1) This Part contains provisions about the amounts (“the elements”) under—
-- src:500 | (a) section 9 (the standard allowance);
-- src:501 | (b) section 10 (responsibility for children and young persons);
-- src:502 | (c) section 11 (housing costs); and
-- src:503 | (d) section 12 (particular needs and circumstances),
-- src:504 | of the Act that make up the maximum amount of an award of universal credit, as provided in section 8(2) of the Act.
@ref reg 23(1) (src:499-504)
GIVEN elements IS AN `Amounts of the elements of an award`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 23(1) — the maximum amount of an award` elements MEANS
    (elements's `the standard allowance`)
    PLUS (elements's `the child element`)
    PLUS (elements's `the housing costs element`)
    PLUS (elements's `the LCWRA element`)
    PLUS (elements's `the carer element`)
    PLUS (elements's `the childcare costs element`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 24: the child element.

-- (1) The amount for each child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible is regulation 36's. The additional
-- amounts of paragraph (2) are counted by the number of disabled children at each rate.
-- src:511 | (1) The amount to be included in an award of universal credit for each child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible ... (“the child element”) is given in the table in regulation 36.
-- src:512 | (2) An additional amount as shown in that table is to be included in respect of each child or qualifying young person who is disabled and that amount is—
@ref reg 24(1) and (2) (src:511-512)
GIVEN `number of children and qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible` IS A NUMBER
      `number of those who are disabled and for whom the lower rate applies` IS A NUMBER
      `number of those who are disabled and for whom the higher rate applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 24 — the amount of the child elements` `number of children and qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible` `number of those who are disabled and for whom the lower rate applies` `number of those who are disabled and for whom the higher rate applies` MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
        ((`number of children and qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible`
              TIMES `reg 36(1) — the amount of the child element for each child or qualifying young person`)
         PLUS (`number of those who are disabled and for whom the lower rate applies`
              TIMES `reg 36(1) — the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `the lower rate`)
         PLUS (`number of those who are disabled and for whom the higher rate applies`
              TIMES `reg 36(1) — the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `the higher rate`))

-- (2) Which rate of additional amount applies to one disabled child or qualifying young person. The five benefits of limb (a) are
-- the core's `Benefit` values; limb (b)(i) names the component and rate of each; limb (b)(ii) is the child or young person who is
-- blind (the core's `reg 2 — blind`). The higher rate takes precedence ("unless sub-paragraph (b) applies").
-- src:512 | (2) An additional amount as shown in that table is to be included in respect of each child or qualifying young person who is disabled and that amount is—
-- src:513 | (a) the lower rate, where the child or qualifying young person is entitled to disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance , child disability payment , adult disability payment or personal independence payment (unless sub-paragraph (b) applies); or
-- src:514 | (b) the higher rate where the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:515 | (i) entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate , the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 , the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations , the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 or the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate, or
-- src:516 | (ii) ... blind.
@ref reg 24(2) (src:512-516)
DECLARE `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount` HAS
    `entitled to`                                                                                                    IS A LIST OF Benefit
    `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Acts and Regulations that define these payments (not a piece)
    `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate`               IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Acts and Regulations that define these payments (not a piece)
    `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Acts and Regulations that define these payments (not a piece)
    `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate`                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Acts and Regulations that define these payments (not a piece)
    `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Acts and Regulations that define these payments (not a piece)
    `sight certificate`                                                                                              IS A `Sight certificate`

-- src:513 | (a) the lower rate, where the child or qualifying young person is entitled to disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance , child disability payment , adult disability payment or personal independence payment (unless sub-paragraph (b) applies); or
@ref reg 24(2)(a) (src:513)
GIVEN child IS AN `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` child MEANS
    (elem `disability living allowance` (child's `entitled to`))
    OR (elem `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (child's `entitled to`))
    OR (elem `child disability payment` (child's `entitled to`))
    OR (elem `adult disability payment` (child's `entitled to`))
    OR (elem `personal independence payment` (child's `entitled to`))

-- src:514 | (b) the higher rate where the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:515 | (i) entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate , the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 , the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations , the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 or the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate, or
-- src:516 | (ii) ... blind.
@ref reg 24(2)(b) (src:514-516)
GIVEN child IS AN `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(2)(b) — entitled to a component at the rate that gives the higher rate, or blind` child MEANS
    (child's `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`)
    OR (child's `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate`)
    OR (child's `entitled to the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate`)
    OR (child's `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate`)
    OR (child's `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`)
    OR (`reg 2 — blind` (child's `sight certificate`))

-- src:512 | (2) An additional amount as shown in that table is to be included in respect of each child or qualifying young person who is disabled and that amount is—
-- src:513 | (a) the lower rate, where the child or qualifying young person is entitled to disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance , child disability payment , adult disability payment or personal independence payment (unless sub-paragraph (b) applies); or
-- src:514 | (b) the higher rate where the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:515 | (i) entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate , the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 , the care component of child disability payment at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations , the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 or the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate, or
-- src:516 | (ii) ... blind.
@ref reg 24(2) (src:512-516)
GIVEN child IS AN `Entitlements of a child or qualifying young person to the additional amount`
GIVETH A `Rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`
`reg 24(2) — the rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` child MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 24(2)(b) — entitled to a component at the rate that gives the higher rate, or blind` child THEN `the higher rate`
        IF `reg 24(2)(a) — entitled to a benefit that gives the lower rate` child THEN `the lower rate`
        OTHERWISE `no additional amount`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 25: the housing costs element. Schedules 1, 2 and 3 are uc3's range.

-- (2) The payments in respect of accommodation must be rent payments (paragraph 2 of Schedule 1) or service charge payments
-- (paragraph 7 of that Schedule). Limb (b) is dots in this text and the text has no "or" between the limbs that are left:
-- they are read as alternatives (fork F-25-2).
-- src:527 | (2) The payments in respect of accommodation must be—
-- src:528 | (a) payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1 (“rent payments”);
-- src:529 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:530 | (c) payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of that Schedule (“service charge payments”).
@ref reg 25(2) (src:527-530)
DECLARE `Payments in respect of accommodation` HAS
    `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1`            IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 1 (piece uc3)
    `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 1 (piece uc3)

-- src:527 | (2) The payments in respect of accommodation must be—
-- src:528 | (a) payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1 (“rent payments”);
-- src:529 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:530 | (c) payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of that Schedule (“service charge payments”).
@ref reg 25(2) (src:527-530)
GIVEN payments IS A `Payments in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(2) — the payment condition` payments MEANS
    (payments's `the payments are rent payments within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 1`)
    OR (payments's `the payments are service charge payments within the meaning of paragraph 7 of Schedule 1`)

-- (3) The liability: the claimant (or either joint claimant) has a liability to make the payments on a commercial basis or is
-- treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having one, and no provision in Part 2 of that Schedule treats them as not liable.
-- src:531 | (3) The circumstances of the liability to make the payments must be such that—
-- src:532 | (a) the claimant (or either joint claimant)—
-- src:533 | (i) has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis, or
-- src:534 | (ii) is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments; and
-- src:535 | (b) none of the provisions in Part 2 of that Schedule applies to treat the claimant (or either joint claimant) as not being liable to make the payments.
@ref reg 25(3) (src:531-535)
DECLARE `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation` HAS
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 2 (piece uc3)
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 2 (piece uc3)

-- src:531 | (3) The circumstances of the liability to make the payments must be such that—
-- src:532 | (a) the claimant (or either joint claimant)—
-- src:533 | (i) has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis, or
-- src:534 | (ii) is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments; and
-- src:535 | (b) none of the provisions in Part 2 of that Schedule applies to treat the claimant (or either joint claimant) as not being liable to make the payments.
@ref reg 25(3) (src:531-535)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(3) — the liability condition` liability MEANS
    `liable on a commercial basis or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2`
    AND (NOT (liability's `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 2 treats the claimant, or either joint claimant, as not being liable to make the payments`))
    WHERE
        `liable on a commercial basis or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` MEANS
            (liability's `the claimant, or either joint claimant, has a liability to make the payments which is on a commercial basis`)
            OR (liability's `the claimant, or either joint claimant, is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 2 as having a liability to make the payments`)

-- (4) The occupation: treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home (with the land used for it),
-- and no provision in Part 2 of that Schedule treats the claimant as not occupying it.
-- src:536 | (4) The circumstances in which the accommodation is occupied must be such that—
-- src:537 | (a) the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home (including any land used for the purposes of the accommodation which is treated under that Part as included in the accommodation); and
-- src:538 | (b) none of the provisions in Part 2 of that Schedule applies to treat the claimant as not occupying that accommodation.
@ref reg 25(4) (src:536-538)
DECLARE `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant` HAS
    `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 3 (piece uc3)
    `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: Schedule 3 (piece uc3)

-- src:536 | (4) The circumstances in which the accommodation is occupied must be such that—
-- src:537 | (a) the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home (including any land used for the purposes of the accommodation which is treated under that Part as included in the accommodation); and
-- src:538 | (b) none of the provisions in Part 2 of that Schedule applies to treat the claimant as not occupying that accommodation.
@ref reg 25(4) (src:536-538)
GIVEN occupation IS AN `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(4) — the occupation condition` occupation MEANS
    (occupation's `the claimant is treated under Part 1 of Schedule 3 as occupying the accommodation as their home`)
    AND (NOT (occupation's `a provision in Part 2 of Schedule 3 treats the claimant as not occupying that accommodation`))

-- (5)(b) A claimant who meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation: the payment, liability and occupation conditions.
-- src:541 | (b) to a claimant who meets the payment condition, the liability condition or the occupation condition are, respectively, to any claimant in whose case the requirements of paragraph (2), (3) or (4) are met (and any reference to a claimant who meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation is to be read accordingly).
@ref reg 25(5)(b) (src:541)
GIVEN payments IS A `Payments in respect of accommodation`
      liability IS A `Liability of a claimant to make payments in respect of accommodation`
      occupation IS AN `Occupation of accommodation by a claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(5)(b) — the claimant meets all of the conditions specified in this regulation` payments liability occupation MEANS
    (`reg 25(2) — the payment condition` payments)
    AND (`reg 25(3) — the liability condition` liability)
    AND (`reg 25(4) — the occupation condition` occupation)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 26: the amount of the housing costs element.

-- (6) A shared ownership tenancy. In England and Wales: a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a
-- percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it. In Scotland: an agreement by which the tenant of
-- accommodation that the tenant and landlord own jointly is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest, or by which the tenant
-- has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest.
-- src:556 | (6) “Shared ownership tenancy” means—
-- src:557 | (a) in England and Wales, a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of accommodation or the cost of providing it;
-- src:558 | (b) in Scotland, an agreement by virtue of which the tenant of accommodation of which the tenant and landlord are joint owners is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest in the accommodation or by virtue of which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it.
@ref reg 26(6) (src:556-558)
DECLARE `Tenancy that may be a shared ownership tenancy` HAS
    `nation in which the accommodation is`                                                                                     IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:556 | (6) “Shared ownership tenancy” means—
-- src:557 | (a) in England and Wales, a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of accommodation or the cost of providing it;
-- src:558 | (b) in Scotland, an agreement by virtue of which the tenant of accommodation of which the tenant and landlord are joint owners is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest in the accommodation or by virtue of which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it.
@ref reg 26(6) (src:556-558)
GIVEN tenancy IS A `Tenancy that may be a shared ownership tenancy`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26(6) — a shared ownership tenancy` tenancy MEANS
    CONSIDER tenancy's `nation in which the accommodation is`
    WHEN England THEN tenancy's `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it`
    WHEN Wales THEN tenancy's `a lease granted on payment of a premium calculated by reference to a percentage of the value of the accommodation or the cost of providing it`
    WHEN Scotland THEN
        (tenancy's `an agreement under which the tenant, who with the landlord jointly owns the accommodation, is the tenant in respect of the landlord's interest`)
        OR (tenancy's `an agreement under which the tenant has the right to purchase the accommodation or the whole or part of the landlord's interest in it`)

-- Which Schedule works out the amount. The answer is a value of the kind below; paragraph (4) is silent on a claimant for whom
-- both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but who does not occupy under a shared ownership tenancy (fork F-26-OVERLAP), which is its own
-- value so that it can be asserted.
-- src:543 | (1) This regulation provides for the amount to be included in an award in respect of an assessment period in which the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25.
-- src:544 | (2) Schedule 4 has effect in relation to any claimant where—
-- src:545 | (a) the claimant meets all of those conditions; and
-- src:546 | (b) the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments (whether or not service charge payments are also payable).
-- src:547 | (3) Schedule 5 has effect in relation to any claimant where—
-- src:548 | (a) the claimant meets all of those conditions; and
-- src:549 | (b) the payments for which the claimant is liable are—
-- src:550 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:551 | (ii) service charge payments ....
-- src:552 | (4) Where both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply in relation to a claimant who occupies accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy—
-- src:553 | (a) an amount is to be calculated under each of Schedules 4 and 5; and
-- src:554 | (b) the amount of the claimant's housing cost element is the aggregate of those amounts.
-- src:555 | (5) But where, in a case to which paragraph (4) applies, there is a liability for service charge payments, the amount in respect of those payments is to be calculated under Schedule 4.
@ref reg 26(1) to (5) (src:543-555)
DECLARE `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element` IS ONE OF
    `Schedule 4 only`
    `Schedule 5 only`
    `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy`
    `neither Schedule, because the claimant does not meet all the conditions of regulation 25`
    `not covered: both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but the tenancy is not a shared ownership tenancy`
    `not covered: neither paragraph (2) nor paragraph (3) applies`

-- src:543 | (1) This regulation provides for the amount to be included in an award in respect of an assessment period in which the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25.
-- src:544 | (2) Schedule 4 has effect in relation to any claimant where—
-- src:545 | (a) the claimant meets all of those conditions; and
-- src:546 | (b) the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments (whether or not service charge payments are also payable).
-- src:547 | (3) Schedule 5 has effect in relation to any claimant where—
-- src:548 | (a) the claimant meets all of those conditions; and
-- src:549 | (b) the payments for which the claimant is liable are—
-- src:550 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:551 | (ii) service charge payments ....
-- src:552 | (4) Where both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply in relation to a claimant who occupies accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy—
-- src:553 | (a) an amount is to be calculated under each of Schedules 4 and 5; and
-- src:554 | (b) the amount of the claimant's housing cost element is the aggregate of those amounts.
-- src:555 | (5) But where, in a case to which paragraph (4) applies, there is a liability for service charge payments, the amount in respect of those payments is to be calculated under Schedule 4.
@ref reg 26(1) to (5) (src:543-555)
GIVEN `the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments, whether or not service charge payments are also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments for which the claimant is liable are service charge payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant occupies the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element`
`reg 26(2) to (4) — the Schedules that have effect` `the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25` `the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments, whether or not service charge payments are also payable` `the payments for which the claimant is liable are service charge payments` `the claimant occupies the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25`)
        THEN `neither Schedule, because the claimant does not meet all the conditions of regulation 25`
        IF (`the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments, whether or not service charge payments are also payable`)
           AND (`the payments for which the claimant is liable are service charge payments`)
        THEN (IF `the claimant occupies the accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy`
              THEN `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy`
              ELSE `not covered: both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but the tenancy is not a shared ownership tenancy`)
        IF `the payments for which the claimant is liable are rent payments, whether or not service charge payments are also payable`
        THEN `Schedule 4 only`
        IF `the payments for which the claimant is liable are service charge payments`
        THEN `Schedule 5 only`
        OTHERWISE `not covered: neither paragraph (2) nor paragraph (3) applies`

-- (4) and (5) The housing costs element: the amount worked out under the Schedule that has effect, or under each of Schedules
-- 4 and 5 added together for a shared ownership tenancy. The amounts calculated under the Schedules are uc3's range, so they are
-- inputs. A case that regulation 26 does not cover, or in which no Schedule has effect, has no amount (NOTHING).
-- src:543 | (1) This regulation provides for the amount to be included in an award in respect of an assessment period in which the claimant meets all the conditions specified in regulation 25.
-- src:552 | (4) Where both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply in relation to a claimant who occupies accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy—
-- src:553 | (a) an amount is to be calculated under each of Schedules 4 and 5; and
-- src:554 | (b) the amount of the claimant's housing cost element is the aggregate of those amounts.
-- src:555 | (5) But where, in a case to which paragraph (4) applies, there is a liability for service charge payments, the amount in respect of those payments is to be calculated under Schedule 4.
@ref reg 26(1), (4) and (5) (src:543-555)
GIVEN schedules IS A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element`
      `amount calculated under Schedule 4` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: Schedule 4 (piece uc3)
      `amount calculated under Schedule 5` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: Schedule 5 (piece uc3)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 26(4) — the amount of the housing costs element` schedules `amount calculated under Schedule 4` `amount calculated under Schedule 5` MEANS
    CONSIDER schedules
    WHEN `Schedule 4 only` THEN JUST `amount calculated under Schedule 4`
    WHEN `Schedule 5 only` THEN JUST `amount calculated under Schedule 5`
    WHEN `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy` THEN JUST (`amount calculated under Schedule 4` PLUS `amount calculated under Schedule 5`)
    WHEN `neither Schedule, because the claimant does not meet all the conditions of regulation 25` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `not covered: both paragraphs (2) and (3) apply but the tenancy is not a shared ownership tenancy` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `not covered: neither paragraph (2) nor paragraph (3) applies` THEN NOTHING

-- (5) In a paragraph (4) case where there is a liability for service charge payments, the amount for those payments is calculated
-- under Schedule 4: true exactly when both Schedules have effect and the claimant is liable for service charge payments.
-- src:555 | (5) But where, in a case to which paragraph (4) applies, there is a liability for service charge payments, the amount in respect of those payments is to be calculated under Schedule 4.
@ref reg 26(5) (src:555)
GIVEN schedules IS A `Schedules that have effect for the amount of the housing costs element`
      `there is a liability for service charge payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26(5) — the amount for the service charge payments is calculated under Schedule 4` schedules `there is a liability for service charge payments` MEANS
    (schedules EQUALS `both Schedules 4 and 5, for a shared ownership tenancy`) AND `there is a liability for service charge payments`
